message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
authors:
  - family-names: Byrd
    given-names: Bryant
    affiliation: "Western Colorado University"
title: "HAPLab Metabolic Analyzer"
abstract: "A web-based data reduction and reporting tool for human exercise physiology testing.
  Integrates Parvo TrueOne 2400 metabolic cart data with blood lactate measurements,
  supporting physiologist-determined ventilatory and lactate threshold identification,
  training zone calculation, substrate utilization reporting, and longitudinal
  session comparison."
version: 2.0.1
date-released: "2026-11-26"
url: "https://github.com/bryantbyrd/HAPLab-Metabolic-Analyzer"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20533547
license: MIT
keywords:
  - exercise physiology
  - metabolic testing
  - ventilatory threshold
  - lactate threshold
  - VO2max
  - Parvo TrueOne
  - sports science
references:
  - type: software
    title: "lactater: Tools for Analyzing Lactate Thresholds"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Mattioni Maturana"
        given-names: Felipe
    version: 1.0.0
    license: MIT
    url: "https://github.com/fmmattioni/lactater"
    notes: "The lactate-threshold methods in HAPLab Metabolic Analyzer are a JavaScript adaptation of this R package."
